is, we can establish that:\n\n$$P(\\xi &lt; -2) =3D p,$$\n\nsince the proba=
bilities of being more than two standard deviations away from the mean are =
equal on both sides due to the symmetry of the normal distribution. Now, le=
t's consider the probability of $\\xi$ being between -2 and 0. We can use t=
he fact that the total probability for $\\xi$ being less than 0 is equal to=
 $\\frac{1}{2}$, as the mean of the distribution is 0 and the distribution =
is symmetric.\n\nThe probability that $\\xi$ is between -2 and 0 can be art=
iculated as the difference between the probability that $\\xi$ is less than=
